nment", "Independent Digital Engine", "Internal Data Extraction"], "answer": 1, "why": "The slide defines IDE and gives Visual Studio and JetBrains as examples."}, {"ch": 1, "topic": "GDD & technology", "slide": 47, "q": "Which is an example of an IDE mentioned in the slides?", "options": ["Hollow Knight", "Pong", "Visual Studio", "Pac-Man"], "answer": 2, "why": "Visual Studio and JetBrains are mentioned as IDEs."}, {"ch": 1, "topic": "GDD & technology", "slide": 47, "q": "What does DCC stand for?", "options": ["Dynamic Code Compiler", "Digital Content Creation", "Distributed Character Control", "Direct Console Connection"], "answer": 1, "why": "DCC is the lecture abbreviation for Digital Content Creation."}, {"ch": 1, "topic": "GDD & technology", "slide": 48, "q": "Which abbreviation is presented as the umbrella term across extended-reality concepts?", "options": ["XR", "GDD", "IDE", "QA"], "answer": 0, "why": "The slides describe XR as the more general term including related realities."}, {"ch": 1, "topic": "GDD & technology", "slide": 48, "q": "What does AR refer to in the reality-technology discussion?", "options": ["Audio Rendering", "Automatic Rotation", "Augmented Reality", "Animated Recording"], "answer": 2, "why": "AR is Augmented Reality."}, {"ch": 1, "topic": "GDD & technology", "slide": 48, "q": "What does VR refer to?", "options": ["Virtual Reality", "Visual Rules", "Voice Recognition", "Version Reversal"], "answer": 0, "why": "VR is Virtual Reality."}, {"ch": 1, "topic": "GDD & technology", "slide": 48, "q": "What does MR refer to in the diagram?", "options": ["Music Recording", "Mixed Reality", "Mobile Rendering", "Mechanics Review"], "answer": 1, "why": "MR is Mixed Reality."}, {"ch": 1, "topic": "Challenges", "slide": 49, "q": "Which is a technical challenge in game development?", "options": ["Optimizing performance across platforms", "Selecting a protagonist’s personality", "Writing a game’s genre list", "Meeting retail marketing targets only"], "a