, "slide": 18, "q": "Which is a spatial/physical part of game state?", "options": ["A release checklist", "An achievement description only", "An object’s location and physical attributes", "Global difficulty only"], "answer": 2, "why": "State includes locations and physical attributes."}, {"ch": 2, "topic": "Game state", "slide": 18, "q": "Which is an object-specific non-spatial game-state value?", "options": ["Angle in the scene", "Position on the map", "Health", "Physical size"], "answer": 2, "why": "Health is explicitly given as non-spatial state."}, {"ch": 2, "topic": "Game state", "slide": 18, "q": "Which is a global non-spatial value?", "options": ["Character x-coordinate", "Difficulty", "A platform’s shape", "A coin’s physical location"], "answer": 1, "why": "The slide gives difficulty as a global non-spatial value."}, {"ch": 2, "topic": "Game state", "slide": 18, "q": "What is the relationship between actions and the game state?", "options": ["State is unrelated to actions", "Actions modify game state", "Only aesthetics modify game state", "Game state exists only after launch"], "answer": 1, "why": "The slide explicitly states actions modify state."}, {"ch": 2, "topic": "Game state", "slide": 18, "q": "How fully must designers specify game state in early designs?", "options": ["State is never needed", "Every variable must be finalized immediately", "Only non-spatial values are allowed", "Only enough to understand interactions; focus on actions first"], "answer": 3, "why": "The lecture advises not over-specifying state at the start."}, {"ch": 2, "topic": "Interactions", "slide": 19, "q": "How does an interaction differ from a player action?", "options": ["It must be activated by a separate keyboard key", "It results from game state rather than being a direct player command", "It always improves health", "It is identical to the game’s genre"], "answer": 1, "why": "Interactions can occur without direct controller input."}, {"ch": 2, "topic": "Interactions", "sl